### status: none
### public: false
### authRequired: true
### sessionAuthRequired: true
### tenantScopedHeadersRequired: true
### destructive: false
### requiresTenantHeaders: true
### llmOperational: false
### protectedContract: true
### referenceOnly: false
### runtimeRecordConfirmed: false
### selectorConfirmed: true
### publishedBackendConfirmed: false
### knownPublishedFailure: false
### selectionGuidance: protected-contract-governed-rule-parameters-read

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8088
@origin = http://localhost:4003
@tenantId = <isolated tenant owning the definition>
@envId = local
@readerSession = <SESSION cookie issued to a RULE_DEFINITION_READER principal>
@definitionId = <definition UUID resolved from the governed definition catalog>

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/praxis/config/domain-rules/definitions/{{definitionId}}/parameters
Accept: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Env: {{envId}}
Cookie: SESSION={{readerSession}}

### Protected contract read; this exact request is not confirmed on the published backend.
### Resolve definitionId from the same authenticated tenant/environment scope as the reader session.
### Response: praxis.domain-rule-parameter-catalog.v1, definitionId/ruleKey/definitionVersion,
### templateKey/templateVersion and typed parameter descriptors (STRING, NUMBER, INTEGER, BOOLEAN).
### Constraints include required/nullable/readOnly, unit, inclusive minimum/maximum and allowedValues.
### origin=DECLARED distinguishes declaredValue:null from an absent declaration using a default.
### An absent defaultValue property means no default; defaultValue:null is an explicit nullable default.
### effectiveValue belongs to the persisted definition; workspace values can differ from that base.
### Definitions without a template return null template identity and an empty parameters list.
### Parameters bind native scalar sites declared in the Engine template. Host var facts keep their meaning.
### This read does not authorize editing the template, facts, condition or other parameter metadata.
### Parameterized changes follow the ETag-controlled workspace and reviewed snapshot lifecycle.
### Generic publications/materializations are not the publication route for parameter templates.
